WEBVTT

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:03.810
Manager.

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.520
Yes?

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.440
About Hanayashiki tomorrow...

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:07.230
Uh-huh?

00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Should we meet at the station?

00:00:09.110 --> 00:00:13.950
Sure. Or would it be better for you to meet at Hanayashiki itself?

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:16.450
No, the station.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.200
I want to meet at the station, see...

00:00:18.450 --> 00:00:19.330
Then at the station it is.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.250
At ten.

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:22.540
At ten. What about lunch?

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:24.710
Are there places to eat at Hanayashiki?

00:00:25.090 --> 00:00:25.840
Sure.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:26.920
Then we'll eat there.

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:32.220
An amusement park?

00:00:32.470 --> 00:00:33.970
Uh-huh! Hanayashiki!

00:00:34.850 --> 00:00:36.640
It looks charming.

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:38.140
Hmm...

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:39.390
You're not interested?

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.310
No, going to an amusement park is okay...

00:00:42.310 --> 00:00:44.940
Then what? You don't like the crowds?

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.190
No, that's... I'll go.

00:00:48.190 --> 00:00:49.400
Let's go.

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.860
There are flowers there, too.

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:51.740
Flowers that I like?

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.740
Well, anyway, I just wanna go.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:57.830
You do drag me all over the place, don't you?

00:00:57.830 --> 00:00:59.410
I'm not "dragging" you anywhere!

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:01.160
We're going together!

00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.460
Yeah. That's right.

00:01:16.600 --> 00:01:19.430
The ghost has been uncharacteristically quiet today.

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:23.140
Well, tomorrow it's sink or swim.

00:01:27.570 --> 00:01:29.400
<i>And I want to make her laugh.</i>

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:34.990
<i>Once in a while, he can be meek, huh?</i>

00:01:44.620 --> 00:01:51.260
I didn't care what our future together would have been like

00:01:51.260 --> 00:01:57.430
as we'd have sat close enough to know the other's feelings

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:03.980
I was prepared for the time you left

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:10.820
but still I found no words to encourage you

00:02:10.820 --> 00:02:17.320
After I embraced you with all I had

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:26.870
a sadness that may well have been our closeness

00:02:26.870 --> 00:02:30.540
filled my heart

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:37.050
Saying goodbye was for the best

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:43.720
You gave me happiness

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:47.060
Until I meet you again one day

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.560
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.110
Summer Snow Rendezvous
Until I know what you are truly like

00:02:52.110 --> 00:02:56.820
I won't forget your smile
Summer Snow Rendezvous

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:57.910
I won't forget your smile

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.760
I'm nervous.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:21.970
Are you?

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.720
Do you feel normal?

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:24.970
Yeah, for now.

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:27.260
It feels different to me.

00:03:27.260 --> 00:03:28.470
Like that cap?

00:03:28.470 --> 00:03:30.060
You don't like it?

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:34.150
Now your hair's messed up.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:36.860
That just made it worse.

00:03:36.860 --> 00:03:38.190
I think I'll wear the cap.

00:03:38.190 --> 00:03:39.690
You don't normally wear one, right?

00:03:40.780 --> 00:03:41.530
No...

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:46.200
Thank you, as always.

00:03:46.410 --> 00:03:49.200
I like the design on your cap.

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:51.870
It's pretty.

00:03:55.210 --> 00:03:59.130
Yeah... caps...

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:03.130
<i>Gimme back my memory.</i>

00:04:08.430 --> 00:04:09.770
Want a beer?

00:04:09.770 --> 00:04:10.640
No...

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.430
It's okay, go ahead.

00:04:12.430 --> 00:04:13.270
What about you?

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.650
I'll pass.

00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:15.400
One.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:16.650
Why don't you have one too, Miss?

00:04:16.650 --> 00:04:17.730
Just the one...

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.230
One beer over here!

00:04:22.030 --> 00:04:25.490
The portions here are pretty generous.

00:04:26.280 --> 00:04:27.570
I'm taking an egg.

00:04:33.120 --> 00:04:35.000
Here, why don't you drink a little too?

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:37.080
Thank you.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.290
Want some?

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:39.750
Okay, just a little.

00:04:43.880 --> 00:04:45.510
<i>I think it's my first time doing this.</i>

00:04:46.890 --> 00:04:49.560
Well, cheers anyway.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.060
It's not like we're celebrating anything.

00:04:51.060 --> 00:04:52.180
For the mood.

00:04:58.230 --> 00:05:00.940
Hanayashiki Street

00:05:04.780 --> 00:05:06.660
<i>Right, this is what it was like.</i>

00:05:07.770 --> 00:05:08.700
<i>It's all coming back to me.</i>

00:05:12.160 --> 00:05:13.700
So this is what it's like.

00:05:13.700 --> 00:05:15.460
You invited me here without knowing?

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:17.420
T-This is my first time here.

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:18.130
Really?

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:20.130
Um, how about taking a photo?

00:05:20.130 --> 00:05:21.460
Sure.

00:05:23.920 --> 00:05:26.300
<i>Well, it is the entrance.</i>

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:28.640
Are you the type of person who often takes photos to mark occasions?

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:31.350
To be honest, I thought you would refuse.

00:05:31.350 --> 00:05:35.890
But I've been feeling really self-conscious since we got here.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.980
Uh-huh. Because this as a date.

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:40.730
Well...

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:41.860
Okay.

00:05:43.820 --> 00:05:45.190
<i>I think I'm gonna cry.</i>

00:05:45.190 --> 00:05:46.530
Are you sweating?

00:05:54.950 --> 00:05:58.040
<i>Even though the first step of getting out of the flower shop is going well,</i>

00:05:59.420 --> 00:06:03.840
<i>why is that bastard of a ghost so fresh in my mind?</i>

00:06:14.680 --> 00:06:19.690
Well, we're here, but let's start by getting a feel for the whole park.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.520
Over there is something I recommend.

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:22.980
Really?

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.230
Let's do that.

00:06:28.360 --> 00:06:30.700
We're starting... here?

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:32.070
Yeah. It's summer after all.

00:06:32.410 --> 00:06:35.740
Couldn't we start with a more fantasy-themed ride?

00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.500
These will be cherry blossom ghosts.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:39.290
That's not what I mean.

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.000
Hazuki, maybe you're a chicken?

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:44.420
I've had my fill of horror...

00:06:45.460 --> 00:06:48.840
How about those potty ducks with the funky faces out front?

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:50.590
Call them "Swan Boats!"

00:06:50.590 --> 00:06:52.800
Oh, those are swans.

00:06:53.050 --> 00:06:55.350
In that case, I think we'd be better off with the pirate ship, right?

00:06:55.350 --> 00:06:56.470
There you go!

00:07:00.480 --> 00:07:02.520
It's cooler up here than I thought.

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:12.860
<i>"Shrine Burabo. Hanayashiki's God of Weddings and Good Matches."</i>

00:07:14.240 --> 00:07:16.080
You can see the Sky Tree!

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:17.660
Let's go there, too.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:18.620
It's crowded!

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:19.960
Okay, when it's not so crowded.

00:07:19.960 --> 00:07:20.620
Yeah.

00:07:25.130 --> 00:07:27.670
We're not up high. It's not scary at all.

00:07:27.670 --> 00:07:28.840
Yeah...

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:29.970
Are you scared?

00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:30.760
No.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.640
That wasn't there back then.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:40.140
Things sure change.

00:07:40.560 --> 00:07:42.770
<i>"Bridge of Happiness.</i>

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:45.860
<i>If you cross it without looking back, your wish will come true."</i>

00:07:47.110 --> 00:07:47.860
<i>Is that it?</i>

00:07:49.480 --> 00:07:50.780
What?

00:07:51.110 --> 00:07:52.400
You looked back.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.740
Well, you called my name.

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.410
Don't you know the deal with this bridge?

00:07:57.240 --> 00:07:59.620
Oh, never mind.

00:08:00.330 --> 00:08:01.040
Carp!

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.790
Look at the carp!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:05.540
They're huge, aren't they?

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:07.460
<i>She looked back twice, so it's reset!</i>

00:08:08.090 --> 00:08:09.250
Yeah, they are huge!

00:08:09.250 --> 00:08:09.920
Yep.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:14.630
<i>No good.</i>

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:19.180
<i>How can I make her smile like in that photo?</i>

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:21.220
<i>Hmm...</i>

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:28.150
<i>Even though we're holding hands as we walk,</i>

00:08:28.150 --> 00:08:30.150
<i>it doesn't feel like anything's gonna happen.</i>

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.650
<i>She even said it was a date.</i>

00:08:33.320 --> 00:08:36.030
<i>Aren't you supposed to be happy and excited on a date?</i>

00:08:39.620 --> 00:08:41.750
What? Need a smoke?

00:08:42.200 --> 00:08:44.290
No, I'm still fine.

00:08:44.290 --> 00:08:45.920
You don't have to hold back.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.580
There's a smoking area over there.

00:08:47.580 --> 00:08:49.790
No, really. It'd be a waste of our time, anyway.

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:51.380
We've got a lot of time.

00:08:52.010 --> 00:08:52.960
Right...

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:58.760
<i>Even if it's just for a little while, I want to be together.</i>

00:08:59.850 --> 00:09:01.770
<i>It's not how I imagined it.</i>

00:09:02.520 --> 00:09:04.430
<i>Is it because of our age difference?</i>

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:07.810
<i>Maybe she's been to Hanayashiki a lot of times.</i>

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:17.240
<i>No, no, no. Screw the cigarettes.</i>

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.620
<i>I've gotta be more proactive! Better get going.</i>

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:28.000
I'll pass on this one. I'll watch from below.

00:09:28.000 --> 00:09:29.000
What?

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:30.170
You two ride it.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.340
What did you come here for?

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:34.090
Did you get done in from that pirate boat?

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:36.300
Just from that? We came all this way, too.

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:38.590
I came to experience the atmosphere.

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:40.680
You two go on it without me.

00:09:41.390 --> 00:09:43.350
I'll wait down here for you.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.850
Let's go on the next one!

00:09:50.400 --> 00:09:51.900
I'll be watching from here.

00:09:51.900 --> 00:09:53.190
You two go on it.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.950
<i>You don't have to tell me. I was going to leave you there anyway.</i>

00:10:14.770 --> 00:10:16.650
<i>Those earrings are humongous.</i>

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.860
<i>Flashy and shiny...</i>

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:22.570
It's empty during the week, huh?

00:10:23.240 --> 00:10:26.160
We're the only ones on this ride.

00:10:26.740 --> 00:10:27.820
<i>They're bright.</i>

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:34.160
Nice view.

00:10:35.960 --> 00:10:40.960
Sh-Should we... sit next... to... other?

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:42.670
The cabin would tilt.

00:10:42.920 --> 00:10:44.170
Yeah, you're right.

00:10:44.170 --> 00:10:46.260
And "next to other?"

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:50.680
Was it always this high?

00:10:51.430 --> 00:10:53.560
Behold, the people below are nothing but specks of garbage.

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:54.930
Balse!

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.310
I wouldn't destroy them.

00:10:58.310 --> 00:11:00.270
I come from a long line of long-lived people.

00:11:00.270 --> 00:11:02.940
So there are merits to being with a younger guy.

00:11:02.940 --> 00:11:04.570
You're still worried about merits?

00:11:04.570 --> 00:11:05.320
Of course.

00:11:05.570 --> 00:11:06.950
You don't need to be.

00:11:06.950 --> 00:11:11.030
Manager, sorry to say, but I'm gonna live longer than you.

00:11:11.030 --> 00:11:12.700
I even drink vegetable juice.

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:14.200
You do seem like the persistent type.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.080
Please call it "tenacious!"

00:11:17.330 --> 00:11:21.170
But we never know what's going to happen.

00:11:21.880 --> 00:11:23.340
I don't think you have to make a definitive statement.

00:11:23.710 --> 00:11:25.340
Yes, I do!

00:11:25.970 --> 00:11:27.880
<i>It's fun to get wooed.</i>

00:11:28.840 --> 00:11:30.800
<i>Despite my age, I feel like I'm walking on air.</i>

00:11:32.720 --> 00:11:33.350
What is it?

00:11:33.720 --> 00:11:34.890
I'm praying.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.890
I should really be doing this at that Burabo Shrine, but...

00:11:37.890 --> 00:11:38.770
Bura?

00:11:38.770 --> 00:11:41.610
If it's true that we can't see what's going to happen,

00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:44.610
then it's possible that you'll lean in my favor, isn't it?

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:46.740
<i>He really is persistent.</i>

00:11:47.360 --> 00:11:51.700
I think someone sang a song about how it's easier to communicate when you're holding hands.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:55.120
I'm kind of overwhelmed by your youth.

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:56.790
Don't act like an old woman.

00:11:57.540 --> 00:12:00.120
I love these rough hands.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:02.090
Wha— Hey!

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:03.500
They're the hands of a hard worker.

00:12:04.130 --> 00:12:06.050
They smell like sunshine.

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:08.130
Please, Hazuki...

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:10.640
That isn't fair!

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:12.800
You shouldn't...

00:12:12.800 --> 00:12:14.260
But you don't hate it?

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:18.020
Why are you being so aggressive today?

00:12:18.020 --> 00:12:19.730
<i>Because the ghost isn't here.</i>

00:12:19.730 --> 00:12:20.900
Tell me why.

00:12:21.560 --> 00:12:25.480
Talking here like this really does make it easier to communicate.

00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:29.030
I understand exactly how I feel.

00:12:30.150 --> 00:12:32.370
<i>I wanna make my move while he's not around.</i>

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:41.250
Manager, how do you feel ab—

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:44.040
We hope you enjoyed the Sky Trip.

00:12:50.010 --> 00:12:51.130
One more time!

00:12:51.130 --> 00:12:52.800
The summer heat's even worse in there.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:54.260
We were having a nice trip, weren't we?

00:12:54.260 --> 00:12:55.970
Summers are all about cool evening air.

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:58.310
Let's go to the haunted house.

00:12:58.310 --> 00:13:01.770
I don't want anything to do with people who get their kicks

00:13:01.770 --> 00:13:03.190
from scaring other people.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:05.190
It'll be cool inside.

00:13:05.940 --> 00:13:08.480
If you don't go with me, Hazuki, I'll go alone.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:09.190
Really?

00:13:10.570 --> 00:13:12.990
What are you going to do? I'm going in.

00:13:12.990 --> 00:13:14.200
I'm gonna pass.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.080
I'll wait here.

00:13:16.080 --> 00:13:17.370
<i>He's pretty stubborn.</i>

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:18.700
Go on ahead.

00:13:25.040 --> 00:13:26.130
Huh?

00:13:26.130 --> 00:13:28.880
You left me behind without even a moment's hesitation.

00:13:28.880 --> 00:13:29.840
Why are you here?

00:13:29.840 --> 00:13:33.800
It'd be totally lame to wait outside like that.

00:13:34.840 --> 00:13:37.640
But my husband was always like that.

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:41.230
He couldn't handle anything spinning, high up, or fast.

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:44.310
He shouldn't've gone to the amusement park then.

00:13:44.310 --> 00:13:45.230
Right?

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:49.730
Hazuki.

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:50.650
Yes?

00:13:50.650 --> 00:13:55.110
Did you invite me here because you heard something from Miho?

00:13:56.240 --> 00:13:56.870
Yes.

00:13:57.700 --> 00:13:59.990
You suddenly suggested that the three of us go.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:02.370
So that's why.

00:14:02.370 --> 00:14:04.330
Was I being mean?

00:14:04.330 --> 00:14:05.540
I don't know.

00:14:06.460 --> 00:14:07.840
But it doesn't matter.

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:13.340
Even if you scribble over memories, they don't disappear.

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:16.640
And there's no point in crying over it.

00:14:18.140 --> 00:14:20.930
<i>That's what she says, but her face tells a different story.</i>

00:14:22.520 --> 00:14:24.480
<i>He goes through all the trouble of getting married,</i>

00:14:25.190 --> 00:14:27.980
<i>then he has to leave his young wife behind.</i>

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:31.530
<i>Fine time for me to be sympathizing with the ghost.</i>

00:14:33.440 --> 00:14:35.990
<i>The manager's tears get me right in the pit of the stomach.</i>

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:39.990
You took long enough!

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:47.420
Hot...

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:50.130
Shaved ice! Want some?

00:14:51.340 --> 00:14:52.710
What flavor?

00:14:52.710 --> 00:14:53.970
Blue Hawaii.

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:58.640
There you are.

00:14:59.180 --> 00:15:00.140
Thank you.

00:15:00.470 --> 00:15:01.260
What's up?

00:15:02.180 --> 00:15:03.140
Nothing.

00:15:05.690 --> 00:15:06.640
I'm sorry.

00:15:07.060 --> 00:15:08.150
For what?

00:15:10.440 --> 00:15:11.980
I guess I still can't...

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:15.400
get over Shimao.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:19.120
<i>I know.</i>

00:15:20.070 --> 00:15:23.910
Just telling me that at this point isn't going to make me back off.

00:15:24.370 --> 00:15:26.290
<i>Even if it's just vanity...</i>

00:15:26.790 --> 00:15:29.170
I'm not asking you to choose between us.

00:15:30.170 --> 00:15:36.550
But now I know that you've chosen me, Hazuki.

00:15:37.130 --> 00:15:38.260
Well, yeah.

00:15:38.970 --> 00:15:43.560
That's what I've been saying all along.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:46.850
<i>Long before I started working part-time at the shop,</i>

00:15:46.850 --> 00:15:49.230
<i>it was creepy how many times I dropped in.</i>

00:15:50.310 --> 00:15:52.020
<i>The first time you spoke to me...</i>

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:54.070
Does this flower blossom?

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:56.070
A little.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:16:00.570
<i>On the way home that day, I jumped up and down three times.</i>

00:16:01.870 --> 00:16:05.200
<i>I'm even prepared to date you with that repellent ghost around.</i>

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:08.750
Can I borrow your body?

00:16:08.750 --> 00:16:09.960
<i>Not yet.</i>

00:16:11.210 --> 00:16:15.840
<i>I'm flesh and blood, and the thing I can do for the girl I love is...</i>

00:16:21.300 --> 00:16:25.640
Manager, will you have sex with me?

00:16:27.310 --> 00:16:28.480
What are you saying?

00:16:29.270 --> 00:16:30.140
<i>She looked at me.</i>

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:35.020
You don't beat around the bush, do you?

00:16:35.860 --> 00:16:38.030
Where did that come from?!

00:16:38.280 --> 00:16:39.280
<i>She's laughing.</i>

00:16:40.820 --> 00:16:42.280
Naturally, that's out of the question!

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:51.420
You don't want to go on any more rides?

00:16:52.000 --> 00:16:52.630
No.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.630
I thought you wanted to go on all kinds of rides.

00:16:55.630 --> 00:16:57.050
You know you can go on as many as you want.

00:16:57.050 --> 00:16:57.800
Yeah...

00:16:59.630 --> 00:17:00.680
I'm okay either way...

00:17:03.760 --> 00:17:06.390
Hey, how about stopping in at the shop?

00:17:07.520 --> 00:17:10.560
I still haven't taught you how to open the shop, have I?

00:17:10.560 --> 00:17:14.060
Now? Even though it's a day off?

00:17:14.060 --> 00:17:16.230
It's still early.

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:18.780
Besides, the sooner you learn it, the better.

00:17:18.780 --> 00:17:19.900
Sure...

00:17:19.900 --> 00:17:20.900
Let's go.

00:17:23.030 --> 00:17:24.030
Hazuki.

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:27.910
<i>The best thing I can do for her...</i>

00:17:32.460 --> 00:17:34.790
Thank you for today.

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:36.880
No, thank you.

00:17:37.670 --> 00:17:41.300
Without a special occasion, I'd probably never get to go to an amusement park.

00:17:41.670 --> 00:17:43.800
Come in. I'll make us some tea.

00:17:44.470 --> 00:17:47.390
I'm gonna buy some smokes first.

00:17:47.390 --> 00:17:48.560
Oh, okay.

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:50.390
I'll be upstairs, so come and get me.

00:17:50.390 --> 00:17:51.060
Yeah.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.220
You're staggering.

00:18:26.390 --> 00:18:27.430
Are you drunk?

00:18:30.770 --> 00:18:33.930
I did my best today.

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:37.650
But I'm still not gettin' anywhere...

00:18:38.190 --> 00:18:38.900
Oh?

00:18:39.480 --> 00:18:40.820
Yeah.

00:18:41.820 --> 00:18:43.610
Gettin' nowhere...

00:18:44.860 --> 00:18:47.910
Do you feel like renting out your body now?

00:18:48.530 --> 00:18:49.990
Yeah, sure.

00:18:50.580 --> 00:18:51.490
Really?

00:18:52.080 --> 00:18:53.200
Yeah.

00:18:53.700 --> 00:18:54.750
You can borrow it.

00:18:55.960 --> 00:18:58.130
You just gave me your consent.

00:18:58.130 --> 00:18:59.630
No going back on your word now.

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:02.630
What a hackneyed miracle. Jesus...

00:19:03.050 --> 00:19:05.510
Poor guy, borrowing strength from alcohol.

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:08.510
I don't need sympathy from a ghost.

00:19:09.050 --> 00:19:09.800
Oh?

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:13.890
Hot!

00:19:14.730 --> 00:19:16.770
And bright!

00:19:28.030 --> 00:19:30.280
I told you it's bright...

00:19:52.140 --> 00:19:54.560
What are you doing? I told you I was waiting upstairs.

00:19:57.140 --> 00:19:59.060
Which do you want, kelp and plum tea or green tea?

00:20:00.730 --> 00:20:02.650
Don't sit there.

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:03.570
Ow...

00:20:04.360 --> 00:20:06.320
Eww, you smell like liquor.

00:20:06.320 --> 00:20:07.320
Were you drinking?

00:20:09.490 --> 00:20:11.030
He was drinking...

00:20:11.320 --> 00:20:12.160
Huh?

00:20:13.120 --> 00:20:13.830
Rokka...

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:17.910
Manager...

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:20.330
Yeah...

00:20:21.040 --> 00:20:23.920
"Manager," huh? It feels weird.

00:20:25.380 --> 00:20:28.470
It's weird, isn't it? Being called "Manager."

00:20:28.470 --> 00:20:30.630
What? That came out of nowhere.

00:20:30.630 --> 00:20:32.090
I'm taking the green tea.

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:33.970
Hey.

00:20:34.470 --> 00:20:35.100
What?

00:20:35.850 --> 00:20:36.600
Hey!

00:20:38.770 --> 00:20:41.600
You can hear my voice, can't you?

00:20:42.400 --> 00:20:43.520
I can touch you.

00:20:44.020 --> 00:20:44.730
You're drunk.

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:46.440
I can touch you...

00:20:46.440 --> 00:20:47.360
Hey.

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.330
Sorry!

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:55.450
That's hot...

00:20:55.450 --> 00:20:57.450
Jeez, you're drunk.

00:20:57.450 --> 00:20:59.120
Take that off. I'll get you a change of clothes.

00:20:59.120 --> 00:20:59.830
Hurry up and wipe it.

00:21:03.420 --> 00:21:04.790
Hazuki.

00:21:05.800 --> 00:21:06.920
I'm flesh and blood.

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:10.380
This body is flesh and blood.

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:25.270
Inside the dreams I always have

00:21:26.400 --> 00:21:31.030
you always smile

00:21:31.030 --> 00:21:35.120
Tell me why

00:21:35.120 --> 00:21:38.990
it won't go away

00:21:38.990 --> 00:21:40.790
I gave you everything

00:21:40.790 --> 00:21:42.620
You gave me everything

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:47.420
Forever and ever
You're everything,

00:21:47.420 --> 00:21:49.090
still my everything

00:21:49.090 --> 00:21:52.300
I love you

00:21:52.300 --> 00:21:55.680
The songs of midsummer days

00:21:55.680 --> 00:21:58.810
are a fleeting miracle

00:21:58.810 --> 00:22:04.770
like the winter snow

00:22:05.900 --> 00:22:11.780
If I hadn't met you

00:22:11.780 --> 00:22:14.990
I wouldn't have felt this sadness

00:22:14.990 --> 00:22:22.500
and nothing would have pressed down on my dreams

00:22:22.500 --> 00:22:28.170
If I hadn't been able to meet you

00:22:28.170 --> 00:22:35.220
I would never have known the tenderness in strength

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:40.350
When I close my eyes

00:22:40.350 --> 00:22:44.350
you're right beside me
